"},"grass":true,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/interior/3806.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":10411},"article":{"headline":"Patrick Crayton and Jacurri Brown connect in waning seconds to lift Rice over Temple 31-27","description":"— Freshman Patrick Crayton Jr. threw a 30-yard touchdown pass to Jacurri Brown with six seconds remaining, lifting Rice to a 31-27 victory over Temple on Thursday night.","story":"PHILADELPHIA -- — Freshman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5265447/patrick-crayton-jr\" target=\"_new\">Patrick Crayton Jr</a>. threw a 30-yard touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4685291/jacurri-brown\" target=\"_new\">Jacurri Brown</a> with six seconds remaining, lifting Rice to a 31-27 victory over Temple on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              Rice trailed 27-24 before Crayton directed an 8-play, 58-yard drive that culminated in the winning touchdown. He completed 5 of 10 passes for 106 yards after attempting only six passes all season.\n\n\r\n              Rice scored 17 points in the fourth quarter to overcome a 24-14 deficit.\n\n\r\n              Temple led 10-7 at halftime and Rice took its first lead of the game on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5207930/d'andre-hardeman-jr\" target=\"_new\">D'Andre Hardeman Jr</a>.'s 46-yard touchdown burst up the middle, making it 14-10 in the third quarter. But Temple bounced back with a short touchdown pass by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5077787/jaxon-smolik\" target=\"_new\">Jaxon Smolik</a> and a 79-yard run by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5296362/de'carlos-young\" target=\"_new\">De'Carlos Young</a> to make it 24-14 heading to the fourth.\n\n\r\n              Rice then went on a 20-play drive covering 55 yards with two fourth-down conversions and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5296697/tommy-bauchiero\" target=\"_new\">Tommy Bauchiero</a> kicked a 37-yard field goal to make it 24-17 with 10 minutes remaining.\n\n\r\n              Temple added a field goal, then <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5145788/gael-ochoa\" target=\"_new\">Gael Ochoa</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5087069/max-mosey\" target=\"_new\">Max Mosey</a> connected on a 9-yard TD pass to get Rice within 27-24.\n\n\r\n              Rice forced a three-and-out on Temple's ensuing possession and Crayton led the winning touchdown drive.\n\n\r\n              Hardeman had 137 yards rushing and Ochoa threw for 88 yards with two touchdowns for Rice (2-9, 1-6 American Athletic Conference).\n\n\r\n              Smolik threw for 110 yards with two touchdowns and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5296364/keveun-mason\" target=\"_new\">Keveun Mason</a> ran for 98 yards for Temple (2-9, 1-6).\n\n\r\n              The game was the first meeting between the programs. It was only the seventh time Rice had played a team from Pennsylvania and only the second time since 1963.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Temple: The Owls play their season finale at Memphis on Nov. 27.\n\n\r\n              Rice: Army visits on Nov. 28 to wrap up the Owls' season. ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-11-20T04:22:31Z"}}